# S5-07 `norandmaps` post-IRET fault-sequence pair, 2026-11-15

Purpose: determine whether the startup-stack write `#PF` signature observed in
counted Stage 4A user-mode runs recurs when Linux address-space randomization is
disabled. Diagnostic single runs only; this is not acceptance evidence.

## Source and inputs

- Worktree/branch: `codex`; source revision
  `65b86251d2ada4d978dc43bfe719c5baed88beab`. The two treatment runs started
  from a clean tree. The later same-binary control ran while only documentation
  evidence edits were uncommitted; no Rust source or executable changed.
- Host: macOS 26.7.1, arm64.
- Release runner SHA-256:
  `90c5db937de8fff1501c1ce24f0b3a35a546b557dbe24c5a73bd24be6d6b343f`.
- Kernel SHA-256:
  `9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e`.
- Initramfs SHA-256:
  `ee9183a4eded3c16a8c6a7a81c6d5bb79be8bb023f793f7cd61694ea2bd3e588`.
- ACPI blob SHA-256:
  `b1ba6078a4d9bc7a8d224980713d8242e4a708743ce4f56093b00a07c631ffaf`.
- ACPI manifest SHA-256:
  `2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2`.
- Each run used the 3,000,000,000-instruction Stage 4A user-mode profile with
  `--linux-norandmaps`, schema-v5 execution observations, and post-IRET selection
  at zero-based `#PF` ordinal 30. Both were marked `diagnostic_not_counted`.
- A matched-length control used the same runner binary and guest inputs without
  `--linux-norandmaps`. Its 33-character nonce makes the full command line 114
  bytes, equal to the 114-byte treatment command lines; the token values and
  lengths differ to compensate for the 11-byte `norandmaps` parameter.

