## Results

Both guests loaded, emitted the exact nonce, and stopped at
`retired=2,999,999,998` with `budget_exhausted`. Each recorded 33 delivered
`#PF`, zero omitted events, and one `#GP(0)`. Their full ordered
`(RIP, access, CPL, error_code)` fault signatures are identical across all 33
events. Neither sequence contains the known startup-stack store RIP
`0xffffffff8271a9c1` (`rep_movs_alternative+0x11`) or the additional
`__put_user_8` RIP `0xffffffff8271ec4d`.

At ordinal 30, both runs instead captured a CPL3 instruction-fetch fault at
RIP/CR2 `0x4000b0`, error code `0x14`. The post-IRET snapshot matched RIP, CS,
CPL and RSP, then translated CR2 to physical `0x443d0b0` through PT leaf
`0x443d025`. The user RSP was `0x7fffffffee10` in both runs. The table-page
physical addresses differed between runs, while the leaf value and translation
matched.

The matched-length control used the same runner binary and guest input hashes,
omitted `norandmaps`, and kept the complete cmdline at 114 bytes. Its nonce is
33 characters rather than the 22-character treatment nonce so that the
command-line lengths match; this is the remaining token-content difference.
The control reached the same budget with 34 complete `#PF` events. At ordinal
30 it captured the CPL0 write at `rep_movs_alternative+0x11`, error code `0x2`,
to CR2 `0x7ffd5195a8d9`. Its post-IRET walk matched the fault context and
translated CR2 to `0x39fe8d9` through repaired PT leaf `0x39fe867`. The first 30
signatures (indices 0–29) match the treatment pair; at index 30 the control
store is replaced by the CPL3 fetch in both treatment runs. The older counted
C/D pair also had the store at ordinal 30 in both runs; C additionally had the
`__put_user_8` store at ordinal 31, while D did not.

This same-binary, equal-cmdline-length control and the repeated treatment pair
provide direct evidence that the startup-stack write fault is sensitive to the
`norandmaps` intervention in this workload. The nonce token differs in value
and length to preserve total cmdline length, and the matched control is one
single run, so this does not prove that every such fault is benign or that the
full counted S5-07 series is reproducible.

The separate automatic `norandmaps` N=2 series still returned
`matches=false` for `machine_observations` and `ordered_uart_bytes`; its RDTSC,
IRQ/quanta and UART differences remain unresolved. These single-run sidecars
were not passed through the series comparator and do not change acceptance or
normalization rules. S5-07 remains blocked/unaccepted.

